      "content": "This intermittent pressure drop sounds like a classic case of a system being slightly out of sync, which is frustrating! It's less like a steady leak and more like a momentary surge or blockage, which could be a tricky piece of plumbing or a sensor acting up. You might want to check the vacuum lines leading to the wastegate actuator or any boost solenoids for tiny, intermittent connections. Sometimes, a loose clamp or a slight vibration can cause a momentary disconnect, mimicking a pressure drop.",
